# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Supabase — required for auth + database
# Find these values in your Supabase project at:
#   https://app.supabase.com → Project Settings → API
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Project URL (safe to expose to the browser)
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://esuatccbicekcohzgcvd.supabase.co

# Anon / public key (safe to expose to the browser; access is governed by RLS)
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.eyJpc3MiOiJzdXBhYmFzZSIsInJlZiI6ImVzdWF0Y2NiaWNla2NvaHpnY3ZkIiwicm9sZSI6ImFub24iLCJpYXQiOjE3ODc4Nzg5MTQsImV4cCI6MjEwMzQ1NDkxNH0.vIHvaQzdgin0eq2o2PEdLbIfOYKBUTi1rPbgp4OgrVw
# Service-role key — NEVER expose this to the browser.
# Required for privileged server-side operations that bypass RLS.
# Found under: Project Settings → API → service_role secret
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.eyJpc3MiOiJzdXBhYmFzZSIsInJlZiI6ImVzdWF0Y2NiaWNla2NvaHpnY3ZkIiwicm9sZSI6InNlcnZpY2Vfcm9sZSIsImlhdCI6MTc4Nzg3ODkxNCwiZXhwIjoyMTAzNDU0OTE0fQ.57N4wEDae6sbI1u5MCGMWghyjNEjRAMFD9vZ42p5w78
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Build orchestrator — required for the chat to build anything
# The n8n workflow behind the chat. See n8n/README.md.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# The production webhook of the "QuickStark.Ai — Build Orchestrator" workflow.
# Deliberately NOT NEXT_PUBLIC_: every build goes through /api/build, which
# checks who is asking and which projects they own. In the browser bundle this
# URL would let anyone POST builds straight to n8n.
# Without it the chat answers "Building is not connected yet" and nothing runs.
# N8N_WEBHOOK_URL=https://<neauraissystems.app.n8n.cloud>.app.n8n.cloud/webhook/api/v1/build

# Sent as the `X-QuickStark-Token` header when set, and checked by the Header
# Auth credential on the Webhook node. Not optional: that workflow writes to the
# projects table with the service_role key, which bypasses RLS, so an
# unauthenticated webhook is a way to overwrite any project row.
#
# Generate one with:  node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('base64url'))" 
# N8N_WEBHOOK_TOKEN=3hkxi0B1FPlXjt8SjbxHS0NmOTzxncFgQQyhx6eezdo
